#   This configuration file pertains only to the instance of yt-dlp which yt-menu manages,
#   not any (if any) system-wide installation of yt-dlp.

#   1. Uncomment and edit your download directory for "Option 4: Normal yt-dlp":
#--paths '/your/chosen/path/here'

#   2. Choose your video resolution:
# Download the video with smallest resolution no worse than [resolution]p,
# or the video with the largest resolution available if there is no such video,
# preferring better codec and then larger total bitrate for the same resolution
# -S "lang" selects for best quality if default audio stream
-S "lang,+res:720,codec,br"

#   The rest of this config is preset with sensible standards:

# Some sites may use naming conventions for Title which are not practical to use as filename (Facebook...):
#--output "%(date)s - %(channel)s - %(ext)s"
# Normal filename structure: Channel - Title.Date.PlaylistNumber (padded with 0 if one digit).FileExtension
--output "%(channel)s - %(title)s.%(upload_date)s.%(autonumber)02d.%(ext)s"

# Restrict filenames to ASCII characters, avoid "&" and spaces:
--windows-filenames

# English subs languages config only, --embed-subs or --write-subs are needed, if neither are present no sub donwload will occur.
--write-auto-subs --sub-langs "en.*"

# Do not exit on error, crucial for downloading subtitles (wherein not finding a specific language results in an error)
-i

# Merge subtitles into video file
--embed-subs

# Embed metadata to the video file. Also adds chapters to file
--embed-metadata

# Download only the video, if the URL refers to a video AND a playlist
--no-playlist

# Number of seconds to sleep before each download when used alone or a lower bound of a range for randomized sleep before each down>
--min-sleep-interval 1
--max-sleep-interval 2

# Number of fragments of a dash/hlsnative video that should be download concurrently (default is 1)
# May interfere with subtitle download in very rare situations.
--concurrent-fragments 4

# Do not overwrite existing output files
#--no-overwrites

# Authenticate using your own cookies from your browser to bypass restrictions
# --cookies-from-browser chrome

## Download all available subtitles
#--all-subs

# Write description (separate file)
#--write-description

# Write comments (separate file)
#--write-comments
